   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I am developing functions to use Google&#39;s Material design in shiny apps.<div><br></div><div><div><div>It appears I can write these functions in 1 of 2 ways:</div><div><br></div><div>#1 Using shiny tags</div><div>e.g.</div><div><div style=\"border-width:1px;border-style:solid;border-color:rgb(187,187,187);background-color:rgb(250,250,250);word-wrap:break-word\"><code><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">materialButton </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,136)\">function</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">inputId</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> label</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">){</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br>  shiny</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">::</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">tags$button</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br>    id </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><font color=\"#000000\"> inputId<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><br>    <font color=\"#000088\">class</font> <span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&#39;materialButtonClass&#39;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><br>    label<br>  <span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span><br><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">}</span></font></code></div><br><br></div><div>#2 Generate HTML strings</div><div>e.g. </div></div><div><div style=\"border-width:1px;border-style:solid;border-color:rgb(187,187,187);background-color:rgb(250,250,250);word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">materialButton </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,136)\">function</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">inputId</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> label</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">){</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">  </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">HTML</span>(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace\">    </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:rgb(102,102,0)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace\">paste0</span>(</span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">  </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">  </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">  </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">  </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">  </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">  </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><font color=\"#008800\" face=\"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\">&quot;&lt;</font><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0);font-family:monospace\">button</span><font color=\"#008800\" face=\"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\">&quot;</font></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">  </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">  </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">  </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">  </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">  </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">  </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&quot; id=&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span> inputId<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><br></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">  </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">  </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">  </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">  </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">  </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">  </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&quot; </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">class=&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&quot;&#39;materialButtonClass&#39;&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><br></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">  </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">  </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">  </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">  </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">  </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">  </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&quot;&gt;&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><br></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">  </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">  </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">  </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">  </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">  </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">  </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">label<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><br></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">  </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">  </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">  </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">  </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">  </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">  </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&quot;&lt;/button&gt;&quot;<br></span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">    </span><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\">)<br></font><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">  </span><font color=\"#000088\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">)<br>)</span></font></div></code></div><br><br></div><div>#1 seems more conventional, however #2 gives me ultimate flexibility.</div><div><br></div><div><font size=\"4\">My question is:</font></div><div>Is there an issue using shiny::HTML (#2) to create functions to generate HTML strings?</div><div><br></div><div>Thank you,</div><div>EA</div></div><div><br></div><div>Note:</div><div>Tags such as &quot;button&quot; did not cause any issues. I ran into an issue when trying to create a &quot;materialSelectInput&quot;. Specifically, assigning which value is &quot;selected&quot; using only shiny tags. If I use HTML strings instead, specifying the &quot;selected&quot; value becomes much more simple.<br></div></div>"
